<%--
Pin_Verification_Form

The PIN-entry worked example: an <Rsx_Form> around a single Pin_Input. It shows that a
one-field form is still a form - the code is checked by the endpoint, and a wrong or
incomplete code comes back as a validation error pinned on the `pin` field.
--%>
<Define:Pin_Verification_Form>

    <Rsx_Form $controller="Dev_Modals_Controller" $method="verify_pin">

        <Form_Errors />

        <Pin_Input $name="pin" $length=6 />

        <div class="text-center text-muted small mt-2">
            Enter the 6-digit PIN code
        </div>

    </Rsx_Form>

</Define:Pin_Verification_Form>
